A||||5||Black88GT||3.4 GT vs. 360 Modena?!?!||||11||
Z||000000||Black88GT||03-18-2001||03:40 PM||||Wow.  I was driving home from work today, really tired sitting at a red light.  All of the sudden, I hear the baddest sounding engine growl I have ever heard in my entire life.  I instantly perked up to look over and see a brand new 360 Modena with a balding old guy gunning the engine.  I was like yeah right is this guy crazy?  I rolled down my window and asked him what he was doing.  He said he just passed the 2,000 mile mark so he wanted to race someone.  I was like do you understand that you have a Ferrari?  Then the light turned green I was left sitting there with a cloud of smoke in my face from his burnout.  Tried to catch him but, it's a Ferrari.  Sorry I just had to tell someone.||||reg||11
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-18-2001||03:52 PM||||You should have gone for it!<P>There is no loss of honor in losing to a Ferrari.  They sound better from behind anyway.  The guy driving a Ferrari would love to hear and see his car kicking ass!  So, in this way, he envied you.<P>I race from trafficlights against 'Vettes with my 2M4 all the time.  I never win, but I always do a lot better than I thought I ever could.  Never discount the possibility that the other driver lacks skill.  Most drivers are faster in automatics, so I always see hope if my oponent is driving a stick.<P>Last thing:  Those smoking Ferrari burnouts cost about $200 each.  I say enjoy the show if you are LuckyEnoughToSeeIt.<P>-LuckTheyWereEverMade||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||03-18-2001||07:21 PM||||If this guy can do it than so can you. He raced a Lamborghini Diablo SV with his MR2. It’s a cool story and the way he words it almost puts you in the driver’s seat.  <A HREF="http://board.mr2pages.com/showthread.php?s=76686725e21a5ee2b8e14fb10d6b73f6&threadid=14528" TARGET=_blank>http://board.mr2pages.com/showthread.php?s=76686725e21a5ee2b8e14fb10d6b73f6&threadid=14528</A>  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||03-18-2001||11:35 PM||||Saw an F355 Spider with the top down going the opposite way on Douglas Drive by my house today.. turned around but got stuck at a light and couldn't find him again.  It was just an awesome sight seeing it come up over the hill in front of me, doing a double-take and then drooling all over myself.  Too bad my radio was too loud, i couldn't hear it... hopefully I'll see it again soon..<P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information<BR>        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: SavedByJebus    -- you'll understand if you watch The Simpsons :D||||reg||1
Z||000004||danny boy||03-19-2001||08:56 PM||||That was the coolest story I've ever heard. I raced a 308 in my 4cyl/5sp once.I kinda lost. I'll be Viper hunting soon.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||03-19-2001||09:14 PM||||I think that was my lucky day in terms of cars.  I also saw a brand new Porsche 911 Carrera, a blue M5 on the highway, and an entire truck full of those new Lexus SC430's.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fieropage/af.bmp"> ||||reg||1
